"ChatGPT — Release Notes | OpenAI Help Center (https://help.openai.com/en/articles/6825453-chatgpt-release-notes)\nciteturn2844view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/6825453-chatgpt-release-notes\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 2685\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChatGPT — Release Notes | OpenAI Help Center (https://help.openai.com/en/articles/6825453-chatgpt-release-notes)\nciteturn2844view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/6825453-chatgpt-release-notes\",\"pattern\":\"October 3, 2025\"}); Total lines: 2685\nL1433: GPT-5.1 Auto continues to route each query to the best model, and GPT-5 models remain available for three months under the Legacy models dropdown so you can compare and transition at your own pace.\nL1434: GPT-5.1 Instant and Thinking are rolling out first to paid (Pro, Plus, Go, Business) users, then to free and logged-out users, with Enterprise and Edu getting a temporary early-access toggle; GPT-5.1 will also be available soon in the API as gpt-5.1-chat-latest (Instant) and gpt-5.1 (Thinking).\nL1435: ## New tone and personalization controls\nL1436: We’re updating ChatGPT’s tone controls so it’s easier to make responses sound the way you prefer. You can now choose from updated presets like Default, Friendly, Efficient, Professional, Candid, and Quirky (with Cynical and Nerdy still available), and we’re experimenting with more granular controls over how concise, warm, or scannable responses are, plus how often emojis appear.\nL1437: Changes you make in Personalization now apply across all chats immediately (including existing conversations), and GPT-5.1 models follow your custom instructions and style preferences more reliably.\nL1438: # November 7, 2025\nL1439: \nL1440: ## Personality and custom instructions now apply to all chats\nL1441: \nL1442: Previously, changes you made to your ChatGPT personality or custom instructions only applied to new conversations. Starting today, updates you make in Settings → Personalization are applied immediately across all chats (including existing conversations!) so your experience stays consistent everywhere without needing to start a new thread.\nL1443: \nL1444: # November 5, 2025\nL1445: ## Interrupt ChatGPT\nL1446: \nL1447: You can now interrupt long-running queries (such as deep research or GPT-5 Pro) to refine what you’re asking—no restart required or progress lost. For example, if you're researching the perfect bookshelf and suddenly remember that your wall is 72\" wide and you can't drill into it, you can simply add that information midstream by clicking “update” in the sidebar and sending the new information as a message. The model will adjust its approach based on your new requirements.\nL1448: # November 3, 2025\nL1449: ## ChatGPT Go Promo - India\nL1450: Eligible customers in India can now get 12 months of ChatGPT Go at no cost. New users can cite116†redeem now on ChatGPT web or the Android app (Google Play). The Apple App Store option arrives next week - no promo code is required for redemption.\nL1451: Available to users in India who are new, on the free plan, or are current ChatGPT Go subscribers - one redemption per account. Requires a payment method (credit card or UPI).\nL1452: If you have an existing ChatGPT Go membership, we may be able to automatically add the promotion for you at the end of your current billing cycle - review cite116†ChatGPT Go Promotion (India) for more details.\nL1453: Update: as of January 21, 2026, the promo has ended\nL1454: # October 30, 2025\nL1455: ## ChatGPT Go expansion\nL1456: \nL1457: We're excited to announce that ChatGPT Go, our low cost subscription plan, is now available in 8 additional countries in Europe, bringing total coverage to cite117†98 countries . The new countries we added are Austria, Czech Republic, Denmark, Norway, Poland, Portugal, Spain and Sweden.\nL1458: For an affordable price, ChatGPT Go provides everything included in the cite73†Free plan, and:\nL1459: \nL1460:   * More messages, larger file uploads, and expanded image generation\nL1461:   * Access to advanced data analysis\nL1462: \nL1463:   * Longer memory for more personalized responses\nL1464: \nL1465: Available on web, mobile (iOS & Android), and desktop (macOS & Windows).\nL1466: Learn more about cite74†ChatGPT Go .\nL1467: ## Credits for Flexible Usage for Codex and Sora\nL1468: \nL1469: Today we’re introducing ways to purchase additional usage in products like Codex and Sora. If you hit your included limits, you can seamlessly buy more credits right in the Codex dashboard or buy more video generations in the Sora app to keep going. Learn more in our article: cite118†Using Credits for Flexible Usage in ChatGPT (Free/Go/Plus/Pro) & Sora. L1470: \nL1471: # October 29, 2025\nL1472: ### ChatGPT Pulse on Web\nL1473: \nL1474: ChatGPT Pulse is now available on web and rolling out to Atlas for Pro users.\nL1475: With Pulse, ChatGPT can do asynchronous research on your behalf once a day based on your past chats, memory, and feedback to help you get things done. The research is delivered to you proactively the next day as a series of visual summaries that you can scan at a glance, expand for more detail, save for later, or ask follow up questions.\nL1476: \nL1477: # October 28, 2025\nL1478: ### ChatGPT Go now available in Brazil\nL1479: \nL1480: We're launching ChatGPT Go, our low cost subscription plan, in Brazil. ChatGPT Go provides everything included in the cite73†Free plan, and:\nL1481: \nL1482:   * More messages, larger file uploads, and expanded image generation\nL1483: \nL1484:   * Access to advanced data analysis\nL1485: \nL1486:   * Longer memory for more personalized responses\nL1487: \nL1488: Available on web, mobile (iOS & Android), and desktop (macOS & Windows).\nL1489: Learn more about cite74†ChatGPT Go .\nL1490: \nL1491: # October 23, 2025\nL1492: ### Shared projects\nL1493: \nL1494: Starting today, project sharing is available to all ChatGPT users, including for Free, Plus, Pro, and Go users globally on web, iOS, and Android.\nL1495: ChatGPT can draw from anything in the shared project – including chats, uploaded files and custom instructions – so responses are informed by your group's internal knowledge, and you can pick up where others left off.\nL1496: Shared projects are ideal for:\nL1497:   * Group work: Upload notes, proposals, and contracts so collaborators can draft deliverables faster and stay in sync.\nL1498: \nL1499:   * Content creation: Apply project-specific instructions to keep tone and style consistent across contributors.\nL1500: \nL1501:   * Reporting: Store datasets and reports in one project, and return each week to generate updates without starting over.\nL1502: \nL1503:   * Research: Keep transcripts, survey results, and market research in one place, so anyone in the project can query and build on the findings.\nL1504: Project owners can choose to share a project with “Only those invited” or “Anyone with a link,” and can change visibility settings at any time including switching back to invite-only. The following collaboration limits apply:\nL1505: \nL1506:   * Pro users: up to 40 files and 100 collaborators\nL1507: \nL1508:   * Plus and Go users: up to 25 files and 10 collaborators\nL1509: \nL1510:   * Free users: up to 5 files and 5 collaborators\nL1511: # October 22, 2025\nL1512: \nL1513: We’re updating the model for signed-out users to GPT-5 Instant, giving more people access to higher-quality responses by default. cite119†See here†openai.com to learn more about the intelligence of GPT-5.\nL1514: \nL1515: # October 15, 2025\nL1516: ## ChatGPT can now automatically manage saved memories so it’s even better at remembering what’s important to you.\nL1517: ChatGPT now manages saved memories automatically by keeping the most relevant details prioritized and moving less important ones to the background. This helps prevent saved memories from reaching capacity and helps avoid “memory full” state in your ChatGPT account.\nL1518: To decide which memories stay top of mind, ChatGPT considers factors such as how recent a detail is and how often you talk about a topic. You can now also search your saved memories more easily and sort them by newest or oldest.\nL1519: You’re always in control: you can turn off automatic memory management at any time, and you can see which memories are currently top of mind and choose to prioritize or deprioritize any specific memory yourself in settings. You can also view and restore prior versions of saved memories.\nL1520: These updates are designed to make saved memory feel seamless, reliable, and easy to manage. We’re beginning to roll this out to Plus and Pro users globally on the web.\nL1522: ## ChatGPT Go expansion\nL1523: \nL1524: We're excited to announce that ChatGPT Go, our low cost subscription plan, is now available in cite117†71 additional countries , bringing total coverage to 89 countries.\nL1525: For an affordable price, ChatGPT Go provides everything included in the cite73†Free plan, and:\nL1526: \nL1527:   * More messages, larger file uploads, and expanded image generation\nL1528: \nL1529:   * Access to advanced data analysis\nL1530: \nL1531:   * Longer memory for more personalized responses\nL1532: Available on web, mobile (iOS & Android), and desktop (macOS & Windows).\nL1533: Note: In Cambodia, Laos, and Nepal, ChatGPT Go subscriptions aren’t available in the iOS app currently. Web and Android subscriptions remain available.\nL1534: Learn more about cite74†ChatGPT Go .\nL1535: # October 13, 2025\nL1536: ## Slack connector and app\nL1537: We’re rolling out two new ways to bring Slack and ChatGPT together: a cite120†connector that brings your Slack context into ChatGPT, and a ChatGPT app for Slack – an integration that enables you to chat with ChatGPT from inside Slack.\nL1538: With the cite121†ChatGPT app for Slack,†intercom.help you can chat one-on-one with ChatGPT in a dedicated Slack sidebar – a space to ask questions, summarize long threads into action items, draft replies, and search messages and files you already have access to. Chats you start in Slack also appear in your ChatGPT sidebar, so it’s easy to pick up later from web or mobile. Semantic search is supported for Slack customers with AI enabled on Business+ or Enterprise+ plans; all other plans use keyword search.\nL1539: With the cite122†ChatGPT connector for Slack†intercom.help , you can securely bring in context from your Slack channels and DMs, making responses more helpful. Available in chat, Deep Research, and Agent Mode. Users can enable from Settings > Apps & Connectors.\nL1540: Both app and connector are available to Plus, Pro, Business and Enterprise/Edu customers. Additionally, the ChatGPT app for Slack requires a paid Slack account; availability and workspace installation may depend on your Slack workspace settings.\nL1541: Installing the app requires the connector to be enabled for your account.\nL1542: Visit the cite121†ChatGPT app for Slack†intercom.help page to get started with installation.\nL1543: # October 9, 2025\nL1544: ## Adding Notion & Linear synced connectors\nL1545: \nL1546: We're adding cite123†Notion and cite124†Linear as synced connectors (for Pro users), so you can securely bring Notion pages and Linear issues/discussions into Chat for fast answers and summaries. You can enable sync for Notion and Linear from your Connector settings (connect to Notion or Linear if you haven’t already, first). Once synced, ChatGPT will automatically reference the indexed content when relevant. Learn more about cite125†synced connectors .\nL1547: # October 8, 2025\nL1548: ## ChatGPT Go expansion\nL1549: \nL1550: We're excited to announce that ChatGPT Go, our low cost subscription plan, is now available in cite117†16 additional countries . For an affordable price, ChatGPT Go provides everything included in the cite73†Free plan, and:\nL1551: \nL1552:   * More messages, larger file uploads, and expanded image generation\nL1553: \nL1554:   * Access to advanced data analysis\nL1555: \nL1556:   * Longer memory for more personalized responses\nL1557: Available on web, mobile (iOS & Android), and desktop (macOS & Windows).\nL1558: Note: In Cambodia, Laos, and Nepal, ChatGPT Go subscriptions aren’t available in the iOS app currently. Web and Android subscriptions remain available.\nL1559: Learn more about cite74†ChatGPT Go .\nL1560: # October 6, 2025\nL1561: \nL1562: ## Updates to Codex\nL1563: \nL1564: We’re rolling out new Codex capabilities to help teams work and build better: cite126†Codex now works in Slack†developers.openai.com , and supports programmatic control through the cite127†Codex SDK†developers.openai.com . Additionally, we've updated cite128†Codex rates .\nL1565: For more information, review our Help Center article on cite99†Codex , and the cite129†Codex developer documentation†developers.openai.com .\nL1566: \nL1567: # October 3, 2025\nL1568: ### Updating GPT-5\nL1569: We’re updating GPT-5 Instant to better recognize and support people in moments of distress.\nL1570: The model is trained to more accurately detect and respond to potential signs of mental and emotional distress. These updates were guided by mental health experts, and help ChatGPT de-escalate conversations and point people to real-world crisis resources when appropriate, while still using language that feels supportive and grounding.\nL1571: As we shared in a cite130†recent blog†openai.com , we've been using our real-time router to direct sensitive parts of conversations—such as those showing signs of acute distress—to reasoning models. GPT-5 Instant now performs just as well as GPT-5 Thinking on these types of questions. When GPT-5 Auto or a non-reasoning model is selected, we'll instead route these conversations to GPT-5 Instant to more quickly provide helpful and beneficial responses.\nL1572: ChatGPT will continue to tell users which model is active when asked.\nL1573: This update to GPT-5 Instant is starting to roll out to ChatGPT users today. We’re continuing to work on improvements and will keep updating the model to make it smarter and safer over time.\nL1574: # September 29, 2025\nL1575: ## Parental Controls\nL1576: We’re rolling out parental controls globally in ChatGPT to help families guide how ChatGPT works in their homes. Available starting on the web today, mobile soon.\nL1577: To set up parental controls, a parent or guardian sends an invite to their teen to connect accounts. After the teen accepts, the parent can manage the teen’s settings from their own account. Teens can also invite a parent to connect.\nL1578: Once a teen is connected to a parent’s account, they automatically receive additional content protections, such as reduced graphic content and viral challenges. Parents will have the option to turn this setting off if they choose, but teen users cannot make changes.\nL1579: Parents don’t have access to their teen’s conversations, except in rare cases where our system and trained reviewers detect possible signs of serious safety risk, parents may be notified — but only with the information needed to support their teen’s safety. Parents can choose if they’d like to be contacted by email, SMS, push notification, or all three.\nL1580: Parents can adjust certain features, set time limits, and add safeguards that work for their family including:\nL1581:   * Set quiet hours, or specific times when ChatGPT can’t be used.\nL1582: \nL1583:   * Turn off voice mode, to remove the option to use voice mode in ChatGPT.\nL1584: \nL1585:   * Turn off memory, so ChatGPT won’t save and use memories when responding.\nL1586: \nL1587:   * Remove image generation, so ChatGPT won’t have the ability to create or edit images.\nL1588: \nL1589:   * Opt out of model training, so their teen’s conversations won’t be used to improve models powering ChatGPT and Sora.\nL1590: ## Introducing Instant Checkout and the Agentic Commerce Protocol\nL1591: We’re introducing Instant Checkout in ChatGPT and the Agentic Commerce Protocol that powers it, built with Stripe.\nL1592: ChatGPT can help you find anything on the web and now with Instant Checkout, you can seamlessly buy directly from the merchant, right in chat. Starting today, U.S. ChatGPT Plus, Pro, and Free users can buy directly from U.S. Etsy sellers through ChatGPT, with over 1 million Shopify merchants, like Glossier, SKIMS, Spanx and Vuori, coming soon.\nL1593: ### Instant Checkout\nL1594: \nL1595: Instant Checkout makes it easy to go from chat to checkout in just a few taps.\nL1596: \nL1597:   * Ask ChatGPT a shopping question and it finds organic, unsponsored product results from across the web.\nL1598: \nL1599:   * Choose an item and ChatGPT shows where to buy, ranking merchants by factors like inventory, price, quality, primary seller status, and Instant Checkout availability.\nL1600:   * If Instant Checkout is offered, tap Buy, confirm shipping and payment details, and pay in one tap with your card on file or other express pay options.\nL1601: \nL1602:   * If Instant Checkout isn’t available, ChatGPT provides a direct link so you can purchase from the merchant’s site.\nL1603: \nL1604: You’re in control at all times and give explicit confirmation to purchase. Payment goes directly from you to the merchant, not through OpenAI. cite131†Learn more about Instant Checkout .\nL1605: ### Agentic Commerce Protocol\nL1606: The Agentic Commerce Protocol (ACP) gives merchants and developers a way to build agentic commerce experiences that work with their current systems and connect them with 700M+ weekly active users on ChatGPT.\nL1607: If you’re a merchant and want to add Instant Checkout in ChatGPT, apply on our cite132†merchant page.†chatgpt.com We’ll be accepting and onboarding merchants on a rolling basis.\nL1608: Developers can start exploring the Agentic Commerce Protocol cite133†documentation†developers.openai.com and example implementations on cite134†GitHub†github.com .\nL1609: # September 25, 2025\nL1610: ## Introducing ChatGPT Pulse for Pro users\nL1611: We’re launching an early preview of ChatGPT pulse for Pro users on iOS and Android. This is a new experience where ChatGPT can now proactively deliver personalized, focused updates for you once a day. These updates are based on asynchronous research ChatGPT can do on your behalf overnight, synthesizing information from your memory, chat history, and direct feedback to learn what’s most relevant to you.\nL1612: Updates are delivered once a day as visual summaries you can scan at a glance or dive deeper into. Each topic opens into more detail where you can ask follow-up questions. You can shape what shows up in pulse with a quick thumbs up or down, or by using curate to tell ChatGPT what you’d like to see.\nL1613: If you ask for something new in the evening, we aim to include it the next morning, though exact timing may vary. Pulse refreshes daily, and you can save any item into a chat to keep it.\nL1664: ## Improvements to search in ChatGPT\nL1665: \nL1666: We’ve made further improvements to search in ChatGPT, making results more accurate, reliable, and useful.\nL1667: \nL1668:   * Factuality: Fewer hallucinations, improving answer quality.\nL1669: \nL1670:   * Shopping: Search is better at detecting shopping intent, showing products when you want them and keeping results focused when you don’t.\nL1671: \nL1672:   * Formatting: Answers are better formatted for quick understanding without losing detail or quality.\nL1673: \nL1674: # September 15, 2025\nL1675: ## Personalization settings are now in Settings\nL1676: \nL1677: Personalization no longer opens in a separate modal. You can manage personalization, choose a ChatGPT personality, add custom instructions, and update Memory directly in Settings → Personalization.\nL1678: ## Updates to Codex (Plus/Pro) - Introducing GPT-5-Codex\nL1679: We’re adding GPT-5-codex, a GPT-5 variant optimized for agentic coding in Codex. It’s available everywhere you use Codex: default for cloud tasks and code review, and selectable for local workflows via the Codex CLI and IDE extension. Use GPT-5-codex for coding-focused work in Codex, or Codex-like environments; use GPT-5 for general, non-coding tasks. Please review the cite136†announcement†openai.com blog for more information.\nL1680: Note: GPT-5-Codex is not currently supported in ChatGPT or the API.\nL1681: To learn more about Codex, visit the cite137†developers site†developers.openai.com as well as our general help article: cite138†Using Codex with your ChatGPT plan .\nL1682: # September 9, 2025\nL1683: ## ChatGPT Voice Update\nL1684: Last month we announced that everyone now has access to Advanced Voice Mode, with usage expanded from minutes per day to hours for Free users, and near-unlimited use for Plus.\nL1685: We also shared that Standard Voice Mode would be retired following a 30-day sunset period. We’ve heard feedback that Standard Voice is special to some folks, and we want to make sure the transition feels right. To that end, we’re keeping Standard Voice available while we address some feedback from its users about Advanced Voice.\nL1686: Stay tuned—more improvements to Voice are coming soon.\nL1687: # September 4, 2025\nL1688: \nL1689: ## Branch conversations on web\nL1690: \nL1691: You can now branch conversations in ChatGPT, making it easier to explore different directions without losing your original thread. Hover over a message, click More actions (⋯), and select Branch in new chat to start a separate conversation from that point.\nL1692: This feature is available today for all logged-in users on web.\nL1693: \nL1694: # September 3, 2025\nL1695: ## Projects Now Available on ChatGPT Free Tier\nL1696: Projects bring your chats and files into one place, helping you stay focused and get things done. They’re now available on our Free tier, with up to 5 file uploads per project.\nL1697: We’ve also updated file uploads on paid tiers: Plus, Go, and Edu support up to 25 files per project. Pro, Business, and Enterprise support up to 40 files per project.\nL1698: New customization options are available for all plans, including colors and icons, to help keep your projects organized.\nL1699: Learn more about cite44†projects in ChatGPT .\nL1700: # August 27, 2025\nL1701: ## Updates to Codex (Plus/Pro)\nL1702: \nL1703: Starting today, Codex works with you everywhere you build—in your terminal or IDE, on the web, in GitHub, and even from the ChatGPT iOS app. Your ChatGPT account connects it all, so you can work seamlessly between your local environment and Codex’s cloud without losing state.\nL1704: We’re excited to introduce the latest Codex updates:\nL1705:   * IDE Extension: The new extension brings codex into VS Code, Cursor, and other VS Code forks, so that you can seamlessly preview local changes and edit code\nL1706: \nL1707:   * Sign in with ChatGPT: Available in both the IDE and CLI, eliminating API key setup and providing access directly through your existing ChatGPT plan\nL1708: \nL1709:   * Seamless Local ↔ Cloud Handoff: Developers can pair with Codex locally and then delegate tasks to the cloud to execute asynchronously without losing state\nL1710:   * Upgraded Codex CLI: Refreshed UI, new commands, and bug fixes\nL1711: \nL1712:   * Code reviews in GitHub: Set up Codex to automatically review new PRs in a repo, or mention @codex in PRs to get reviews and suggested fixes\nL1713: Additionally, all product information and updates for Codex moving forward will be announced on our new site: cite137†developers.openai.com/codex†developers.openai.com .\nL1714: We invite you to explore the site for more details on these new features, as well as guides on how to get started.\nL1715: To learn more about Codex, visit the new cite137†developers site†developers.openai.com as well as our general help article: cite138†Using Codex with your ChatGPT plan .\nL1716: # August 22, 2025\nL1717: ## Project-only memory\nL1718: An improvement to cite44†projects is now available. When creating a project, users have the option to enable project-only memory.\nL1719: With project-only memory enabled, ChatGPT can use other conversations in that project for additional context, and won’t use your cite139†saved memories from outside the project to shape responses. Additionally, it won’t carry anything from the project into future chats outside of the project.\nL1720: This creates a focused, self-contained space, which is useful for long-running or sensitive work where you want ChatGPT to stay anchored to that project’s tone, context, and history.\nL1721: Note:\nL1722:   * Personal Memory must be enabled to utilize this feature.\nL1723: \nL1724:     * Settings -> Personalization -> Memory\nL1725: \nL1726:   * This feature will initially only be available on the ChatGPT website and Windows app. Support for mobile (iOS and Android) and macOS app will follow in the coming weeks.\nL1727: \nL1728: Learn more about cite140†memory in projects .\nL1729: # August 18, 2025\nL1730: ## Introducing ChatGPT Go\nL1731: \nL1732: We’re launching ChatGPT Go, a new low-cost subscription plan. This will initially be available for users in India only.\nL1733: For ₹399/month (GST included), ChatGPT Go provides everything included in the cite73†Free plan , and:\nL1734: \nL1735:   * More messages, larger file uploads, and expanded image generation\nL1736: \nL1737:   * Access to advanced data analysis\nL1738: \nL1739:   * Longer memory for more personalized responses\nL1740: Available on web, mobile (iOS & Android), and desktop (macOS & Windows).\nL1741: ChatGPT Go is geo-restricted to India at launch, and is able to be subscribed to by credit card or UPI.\nL1742: Learn more about cite74†ChatGPT Go .\nL1743: # August 15, 2025\nL1744: ## GPT-5 Updates\nL1961: This upgrade to Advanced Voice is available for all paid users across markets and platforms—just tap the Voice icon in the message composer to get started.\nL1962: This update is in addition to improvements we made earlier this year to ensure fewer interruptions and improved accents.\nL1963: ### Known Limitations\nL1964: In testing, we've observed that this update may occasionally cause minor decreases in audio quality, including unexpected variations in tone and pitch. These issues are more noticeable with certain voice options. We expect to improve audio consistency over time.\nL1965: Additionally, rare hallucinations in Voice Mode persist with this update, resulting in unintended sounds resembling ads, gibberish, or background music. We are actively investigating these issues and working toward a solution.\nL1966: # June 4, 2025\nL1967: ## Connectors in beta for deep research (Plus, Pro, Team, Enterprise, Edu)\nL1968: \nL1969: ChatGPT Team, Enterprise, and Edu customers globally can use connectors in deep research, as well as Pro and Plus users (excluding users in Switzerland, EEA, and the UK) to generate long-form, cited responses that include your company’s internal tools.\nL1970: \nL1971:   * Supported connectors: Google Drive, SharePoint, Dropbox, Box, Outlook, Gmail, Google Calendar, Linear, GitHub, HubSpot, and Teams\nL1972:   * Combines internal + web sources for synthesis\nL1973: \nL1974: Learn more about cite158†Connectors in ChatGPT .\nL1975: ## Custom connectors via Model Context Protocol (Pro, Team, Enterprise, Edu)\nL1976: \nL1977: Admins and users can now build and deploy custom connectors to proprietary systems using Model Context Protocol (MCP).\nL1978: \nL1979:   * Requires a remote MCP server\nL1980: \nL1981:   * Available only in deep research\nL1982: \nL1983:   * Admin-published connectors appear in the connector list for all users\nL1984: Learn more about cite159†building custom connectors with MCP†platform.openai.com . For Team, Enterprise, and Edu plans, only admins can build and deploy custom connectors.\nL1985: # June 3, 2025\nL1986: \nL1987: ## Memory is now more comprehensive for Free users\nL1988: \nL1989: Memory improvements are starting to roll out to Free users. In addition to the saved memories that were there before, ChatGPT now references your recent conversations to deliver responses that feel more relevant and tailored to you.\nL1990: Free users must be logged in and on up-to-date apps (iOS/Android v1.2025.147+).\nL1991: ### Opt‑in reminders\nL1992: \nL1993:   * Free users in EEA (EU + UK), Switzerland, Norway, Iceland, or Liechtenstein will see a prompt to enable this setting or can visit Settings > Personalization > Memory > Reference chat history to enable.\nL1994: \nL1995:   * Outside the European regions listed above, all Free users that have memory enabled will receive the upgrade automatically.\nL1996: \nL1997: You can turn off memory anytime in settings. Learn more in our cite160†Memory FAQ .\nL1998: \nL1999: # May 15, 2025\nL2000: ## Dropbox connector for deep research for Plus/Pro/Team\nL2001: \nL2002: ChatGPT deep research with Dropbox is available globally to Team users. It is also gradually rolling out to Plus and Pro users, except for those in the EEA, Switzerland, and the UK. Enterprise user access will be announced at a later date.\nL2003: See: cite161†Connect apps to ChatGPT deep research L2004: \nL2005: ## GitHub connector for deep research\nL2006: \nL2007: The GitHub connector is now available globally to Plus/Pro/Team users, including those in the EEA, Switzerland, and the UK.\nL2008: # May 14, 2025\nL2009: ## Releasing GPT-4.1 in ChatGPT for all paid users\nL2010: Since its launch in the API in April, GPT-4.1 has become a favorite among developers—by popular demand, we’re making it available directly in ChatGPT.\nL2011: GPT-4.1 is a specialized model that excels at coding tasks. Compared to GPT-4o, it's even stronger at precise instruction following and web development tasks, and offers an alternative to OpenAI o3 and OpenAI o4-mini for simpler, everyday coding needs.\nL2012: Starting today, Plus, Pro, and Team users can access GPT-4.1 via the \"more models\" dropdown in the model picker. Enterprise and Edu users will get access in the coming weeks. GPT-4.1 has the same rate limits as GPT-4o for paid users.\nL2013: ## Introducing GPT-4.1 mini, replacing GPT-4o mini, in ChatGPT for all users\nL2014: GPT-4.1 mini is a fast, capable, and efficient small model, delivering significant improvements compared to GPT-4o mini—in instruction-following, coding, and overall intelligence. Starting today, GPT-4.1 mini replaces GPT-4o mini in the model picker under \"more models\" for paid users, and will serve as the fallback model for free users once they reach their GPT-4o usage limits. Rate limits remain the same.\nL2015: Evals for GPT-4.1 and GPT-4.1 mini were originally shared in the cite162†blog post†openai.com accompanying their API release. They also went through standard safety evaluations. Detailed results are available in the newly launched cite163†Safety Evaluations Hub†openai.com .\nL2016: # May 12, 2025\nL2017: \nL2018: ## Microsoft SharePoint and OneDrive connector for deep research for Plus/Pro/Team\nL2019: \nL2020: ChatGPT deep research with SharePoint and OneDrive is available globally to Team users. It is also gradually rolling out to Plus and Pro users, except for those in the EEA, Switzerland, and the UK. Enterprise user access will be announced at a later date.\nL2021: See: cite164†Connecting SharePoint and Microsoft OneDrive to ChatGPT deep research L2022: ## Export Deep Research as PDF for Plus/Pro/Team\nL2023: \nL2024: You can now export your deep research reports as well-formatted PDFs—complete with tables, images, linked citations, and sources.\nL2025: To use, click the share icon and select 'Download as PDF.' It works for both new and past reports.\nL2026: \nL2027: # May 8, 2025\nL2028: ## GitHub connector for deep research for Plus/Pro/Team\nL2029: \nL2030: ChatGPT deep research with GitHub is available globally to Team users. It is also gradually rolling out to Plus and Pro users, except for those in the EEA, Switzerland, and the UK. Enterprise user access will be announced at a later date.\nL2031: See: cite165†Connecting GitHub to ChatGPT deep research .\nL2032: ## Enhanced Memory in ChatGPT (including EU) on Plus/Pro\nL2033: \nL2034: Enhanced memory rolling out to all Plus and Pro users (including the EU). The new memory features are available in the EEA (EU + UK), Switzerland, Norway, Iceland, or Liechtenstein. These features are OFF by default and must be enabled in  Settings > Personalization > Reference  Chat  History.\nL2035: \nL2036: ### Plan differences\nL2037: \nL2038: • Saved  memories and Chat history are offered only to Plus and Pro accounts.\nL2039: • Free‑tier users have access to Saved  memories only.\n"
